# Forbidden scope residual closure (Wave A)

## Context

Canonical npm scope is **`@app-tour/*`** (Phase 1). Hostile architecture audit (`TEMP/ARCHITECTURE_AUDIT_FINAL.md`) found remaining **`@app-cloud/*` package imports** on API auth/tenant ingress and a few specs — critical because resolution may depend on stale symlinks or fail under clean `pnpm install`.

This tranche does **not** rename ops paths (`/opt/app-cloud`, k8s namespace labels, `Symbol.for("app-cloud.*")`) — those are deployment/runtime identifiers, not TypeScript module specifiers.

## Goal path (Auditor → target architecture)

| Wave | Focus | Outcome lever |
| ---- | ----- | ------------- |
| **A (this)** | Zero `@app-cloud/` **module** imports in `apps/` + `packages/` TS/TSX (+ enforce guard) | Namespace hygiene → ~100% for package specs |
| **B** | Client bootstrap Map → codegen; kill sync `getDenaliWorkspacePlugin` in web | Thin shell / runtime model |
| **C** | Portal/marketing `transpilePackages` + guest-runtime dep graph | Bundle isolation |
| **D** | Plugin export surface + hard-coded `pluginId` branches | Encapsulation / drop-in DX |

## Decision (Wave A)

1. Replace every `@app-cloud/<pkg>` **import specifier** in application/package TypeScript with `@app-tour/<pkg>`.
2. Align e2e/contract assertions that required the forbidden scope.
3. Add `pnpm run guard:no-app-cloud-imports` — fails if `@app-cloud/` appears in `apps/**` or `packages/**` for `*.{ts,tsx,js,mjs,cjs}` (exclude `node_modules`, `dist`, `.next`). Allowlist: none for package imports. Docs under `docs/` are out of scope for this guard (historical Markdoc may still mention the typo).

## Verify

```bash
pnpm run guard:no-app-cloud-imports
rg '@app-cloud/' apps packages -g '*.{ts,tsx}' -g '!**/node_modules/**'
node --test scripts/test/p4-cold-path-fan-in.spec.mjs
```

## Residual (closed in Wave H.k)

Hostile re-audit found codegen still emitting `@app-cloud/*` in admin `transpilePackages` platform set — fixed in [`wave-h-audit-critical-hygiene.mdoc`](./wave-h-audit-critical-hygiene.mdoc).

## Out of scope

- Renaming deploy unit prefixes / Prometheus `namespace="app-cloud"`
- Changing `Symbol.for("app-cloud.requestJwtSessionVersion")` (would break in-flight session attach across mixed builds)
- Shell Denali extraction (Wave B+)

## CI regression note (required gates)

Stale local `node_modules/@app-cloud/*` symlinks can mask forbidden imports on developer machines. Fresh CI has only `@app-tour/*` links from `package.json`, so any remaining `@app-cloud/` specifier fails with `TS2307` during `workspace-denali` / plugin builds (Phase 0 integration, Phase 1, booking-postgres-gate). Prefer `pnpm run guard:no-app-cloud-imports` before relying on a green local `tsc`.
